From: CIRCT STA integration
Subject: [PATCH] timer: endpoint enumeration and when-variant retention

Upstream OpenTimer reports worst paths but offers no public API to
enumerate every analyzed endpoint (pin, split, transition) with its
arrival, required, and slack. Path tracing only materializes violated
paths, so full-coverage aggregates (WNS/TNS/failing over all
constrained endpoints) cannot be built from report_timing alone.

Add Timer::report_endpoints(), which returns one record per analyzed
endpoint after _update_endpoints(), reading the same _endpoints store
that backs report_wns/report_tns/report_fep. No tracing, no new
analysis, deterministic ordering left to the caller.

Retain every Liberty timing variant instead of merging by related_pin
alone, so state-dependent (`when`) arcs all reach propagation (which
maxes over fanin arcs for setup/max, matching worst-case STA). Power-only
placeholders still merge to avoid phantom duplication.

Applies to OpenTimer 2.0 (cd0565fc).

--- a/ot/timer/timer.hpp	2026-09-22 01:33:07.798535207 -0700
+++ b/ot/timer/timer.hpp	2026-09-22 01:33:07.788965312 -0700
@@ -63,6 +63,21 @@
     Timer& set_voltage_unit(volt_t);
     Timer& set_power_unit(watt_t);
 
+    // Struct: EndpointInfo
+    // One analyzed endpoint: pin name plus split/transition identity
+    // with arrival, required, and slack. Arrival or required may be
+    // absent when the timer did not compute them; slack is always
+    // present for analyzed endpoints.
+    struct EndpointInfo {
+      std::string pin;
+      Split split;
+      Tran transition;
+      std::optional<float> arrival;
+      std::optional<float> required;
+      float slack;
+    };
+
+    std::vector<EndpointInfo> report_endpoints();
     Timer& set_current_unit(ampere_t);
 
     // Action.
